hls: an init section the list cannot take is freed, the list kept

new_init_section() added the section with dynarray_add(), which, when it
cannot grow the list, frees the list, sets its count to 0 and returns
nothing: the section was returned all the same, not in the list, and
the sections listed before leaked. Its callers that then drop the
section just added (an EXT-X-MAP key address that is invalid or could
not be copied, and 0103's dedup_init_section()) took the element before
the start of the freed list, a read out of bounds and a free of
whatever pointer it held.

Add it with av_dynarray_add_nofree() and check it: on failure the list
is kept, the section is freed and new_init_section() returns NULL,
which its caller reports as ENOMEM. drop_last_init_section() leaves an
empty list alone; it is only called after a section was added, and a
broken invariant should not abort the process playing the stream (an
av_assert0) nor index the list.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -615,16 +615,28 @@ static struct segment *new_init_section(struct playlist *pls,
         sec->size = -1;
     }
 
-    dynarray_add(&pls->init_sections, &pls->n_init_sections, sec);
+    /* dynarray_add() frees the whole list when it cannot grow it, and
+     * leaves sec to leak and its callers to drop an element it no longer
+     * has: keep the list and fail */
+    if (av_dynarray_add_nofree(&pls->init_sections, &pls->n_init_sections, sec) < 0) {
+        av_freep(&sec->url);
+        av_free(sec);
+        return NULL;
+    }
 
     return sec;
 }
 
 /* The section just added, which the playlist's list holds and frees, is
- * dropped from it. */
+ * dropped from it. Only called after new_init_section() added one; an empty
+ * list is left alone rather than aborting the caller's process. */
 static void drop_last_init_section(struct playlist *pls)
 {
-    struct segment *sec = pls->init_sections[--pls->n_init_sections];
+    struct segment *sec;
+
+    if (pls->n_init_sections <= 0)
+        return;
+    sec = pls->init_sections[--pls->n_init_sections];
 
     av_freep(&sec->key);
     av_freep(&sec->url);
